**Final Answer:**
The fetus may be affected by Hb S/β+ thalassaemia compound heterozygosity, Hb S heterozygote, or have no affected phenotype, depending on the carrier status of the fetus. The fetus may also be affected by β-thalassaemia heterozygote, depending on the carrier status of the fetus. 

