   - Nitrogen: \( 0.21 \times 100 = 21 \)  
   The empirical formula is \( \text{C}_5 \text{H}_6 \text{N}_2 \).

2. **Determine the molecular formula:**  
   The empirical formula mass is:  
   \( 5 \times 12 + 6 \times 1 + 2 \times 14 = 60 + 6 + 28 = 94 \)  
   The ratio of the molar mass to the empirical formula mass is:  
   \( \frac{108}{94} \approx 1.15 \)  
