Since the equilibrium constant is very large, the reaction will shift almost completely to the right, forming almost all of the FeCN$_6^{4-}$. Therefore, we can assume that $x$ is very small compared to 1.0 and 0.25. This allows us to approximate the equation as:

$$1.2 \times 10^{20} \approx \frac{[\text{Fe(CN)}_6^{4-}]}{(1.0)(0.25)^6}$$

Solving for $[\text{Fe(CN)}_6^{4-}]$:

