To find the heat released for 2.5 moles of propane, we can use the following equation:

Heat released = (moles of propane) × (standard enthalpy of combustion per mole)

Heat released = (2.5 moles) × (-2220 kJ/mol)

Heat released = -5550 kJ

The negative sign indicates that the heat is released, as it is an exothermic reaction.

So, the amount of heat released when 2.5 moles of propane is completely burned in oxygen gas is 5550 kJ.
