","a) **Retrospective** - The study examines current smoking status and smoking history of patients who already have been diagnosed with bladder cancer.  
b) **Cross-sectional** - The study records eating habits and health status at a single point in time.  
c) **Prospective** - The study observes the eating and exercise patterns of a group over time to predict future cancer risk.  
d) **Cross-sectional** - The study compares prices of generic and non-generic products at a specific point in time.  

**Explanation:**  
- **Cross-sectional studies** measure variables at a single point in time.  
- **Retrospective studies** involve examining data about an event (e.g., cancer) and its potential causes from a prior time.  
- **Prospective studies** involve tracking a group over time to observe the occurrence of an event (e.g., cancer) and its relationship to factors like eating and exercise.  

The answer (d) is a comparison of existing data (prices) at a specific time, so it is **cross-sectional**.  

\boxed{a: \text{Retrospective}, b: \text{Cross-sectional}, c: \text{Prospective}, d: \text{Cross-sectional}}
