Prove that condition (i) implies condition (ii) in Theorem 29.1, where:  
(i) \( \lim_n \int f \, d\mu_n = \int f \, d\mu \) for all bounded continuous \( f \);  
(ii) \( \limsup_n \mu_n(C) \leq \mu(C) \) for all closed sets \( C \).<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","To prove that condition (i) implies condition (ii), we proceed as follows:  

1. **Define \( C \) as a closed set.**  
2. **Define \( f_C \) as a function defined as:**  
   \[
   f_C(x) = \begin{cases} 
   1 & \text{if } x \in C, \\
   0 & \text{if } x \notin C.
   \end{cases}
   \]  
   This function is bounded and continuous, as it is a constant function on both \( C \) and its complement.  

3. **Evaluate the integral of \( f_C \) under the two measures:**  
   \[
   \int f_C \, d\mu_n = \mu_n(C) \quad \text{and} \quad \int f_C \, d\mu = \mu(C).
   \]  
