Next, compute the second derivatives:
\[
\frac{\partial^2 U}{\partial r^2} = \frac{4 \sin \theta (1 - r^2)}{1 - r^2 + 4r^2 \sin^2 \theta} \cdot \frac{d}{dr} \left( \frac{1}{1 - r^2 + 4r^2 \sin^2 \theta} \right),
\]
\[
\frac{\partial^2 U}{\partial \theta^2} = \frac{4r \cos \theta (1 - r^2)}{1 - r^2 + 4r^2 \sin^2 \theta} \cdot \frac{d}{d\theta} \left( \frac{1}{1 - r^2 + 4r^2 \sin^2 \theta} \right).
\]
