","Let the radius of the cone be \( r \). The lateral surface area of the cone is given by \(\pi r\) (the circumference of the base times the slant height).  
\[
\pi r = \frac{3}{8}\pi \implies r = \frac{3}{8}.
\]
The unfolded diagram of the cone is a sector of a circle with radius 1 and central angle \(\theta\). The length of the sector is equal to the circumference of the base of the cone, which is \(2\pi r = \frac{3\pi}{4}\).  
\[
\frac{\theta}{360^\circ} \cdot 2\pi = \frac{3\pi}{4} \implies \theta = \frac{3\pi}{4} \cdot \frac{360^\circ}{2\pi} = \frac{540^\circ}{4} = 135^\circ.
\]
Thus, the central angle is \(\boxed{135^\circ}\).
