<start_of_turn>model
","1. **Heat Transfer Calculation:**  
   The rate of heat transfer \( q \) to the plate is given by:  
   \[
   q = C_p \rho u \left( T_w - T \right) \left( \frac{1}{2} \right) \left( \frac{1}{2} \right) \left( \frac{1}{2} \right) \left( \frac{1}{2} \right)
   \]  
   Substituting the given values:  
   \[
   C_p = 1.005 \, \text{Btu/lb·°R} = 4.18 \, \text{kJ/kg·°C}
   \]  
   \[
   \rho = 1.000 \, \text{kg/m}^3 \quad \text{(from properties of air at 500°C and 1 atm)}
   \]  
   \[
   u = \frac{40,000}{1.000 \times 0.2} = 200 \, \text{m/s}
   \]  
   \[
   T_w = 100°C
   \]  
   \[
   T = 50°C
   \]  
   \[
   \frac{1}{2} \left( \frac{1}{2} \right) \left( \frac{1}{2} \right) \left( \frac{1}{2} \right) = 0.0125
   \]  
   \[
   q = 4.18 \times 1.000 \times 200 \times (100 - 50) \times 0.0125 = 104.5 \, \text{kW}
   \]  

