\[ \text{Pb(s)} + \text{PbO}_2(s) + 2\text{H}^+(aq) + 2\text{e}^- \rightarrow 2\text{Pb(OH)}_2(s) \]
This reaction can be broken down into two half-reactions:
1. **Oxidation at the anode (Pb electrode):**
   \[ \text{Pb(s)} + \text{H}^+(aq) + \text{e}^- \rightarrow \text{Pb(OH)}_2(s) \]
2. **Reduction at the cathode (PbO₂ electrode):**
   \[ \text{PbO}_2(s) + 2\text{H}^+(aq) + 2\text{e}^- \rightarrow \text{Pb(OH)}_2(s) \]
These half-reactions are combined to give the net reaction.
